expression: output
---
extends — Adds a type bound; it is not interface inheritance.

Syntax:
  class Box<T extends Named> {
    value: T
  }
  
  function take<I extends Iterator<Item = int>>(it: I) -> I.Item? {
    return it.next()
  }
  
  interface Graph {
    type Edge extends Named
  }

Use `extends` in generic parameter bounds and associated type bounds. Do not write `interface Child extends Parent`; interfaces compose with `requires`.
